          "guid": "mssmb5d26py033is",
          "message": {
            "text": "CSS SVG reference filters now receive Chromium's element-local coordinate space. Blink builds these filters against a zero-origin reference box, whereas applying the captured definition directly to an absolute-coordinate SVG group made userSpaceOnUse primitives sample root coordinates; the translate/counter-translate wrapper changes only the filter coordinate system and preserves page placement. The focused 07-deep fixture improved from major (17 regions, 0.12%) to trivial (2 regions, 0.01%), eliminating both displacement mismatches.",
            "markdown": "CSS SVG reference filters now receive Chromium's element-local coordinate space. Blink builds these filters against a zero-origin reference box, whereas applying the captured definition directly to an absolute-coordinate SVG group made userSpaceOnUse primitives sample root coordinates; the translate/counter-translate wrapper changes only the filter coordinate system and preserves page placement. The focused 07-deep fixture improved from major (17 regions, 0.12%) to trivial (2 regions, 0.01%), eliminating both displacement mismatches."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "src/render/element-tree-to-svg.ts"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 3638,
                  "endLine": 3646,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "  // Chromium builds CSS URL-reference filters on HTML elements against a\n  // reference box whose origin is local to the filtered element. An SVG <g>,\n  // however, exposes its root-space bbox to userSpaceOnUse primitives. That\n  // difference is visible with coordinate-sensitive primitives such as\n  // feTurbulence/feDisplacementMap. Put reference filters on a translated\n  // outer wrapper and counter-translate their content so the filter sees the\n  // same local coordinate space while the result stays at its page position.\n  const localizeReferenceFilter = /\\burl\\(\\s*(?:[\"']?)#/i.test(filterCss);\n  const needsFilterOuter = filterCss !== \"\" && (localizeReferenceFilter || clipPathUrlId != null || maskUrlId != null);"
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "tags": [
              "rationale"
            ],
            "ext-ai-tool-confidence": 0.98
          },
